::GEO_U04_L05_Q11::
Question ID: GEO_U04_L05_Q11
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only
Question:
A right triangle has hypotenuse 5 and one leg 3. What is the other leg?
{
~A. 2#Subtracting side lengths ignores the squared relationship.
=B. 4#Use b? = 5? - 3?; the missing leg is 4.
~C. 8#Adding the known lengths does not find a missing leg.
~D. sqrt(34)#Adding squares would be used if both known sides were legs, but 5 is the hypotenuse.
}
